          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What screening tool does guidance describe for anxiety, and what does the score change?",
          "answer": "The seven-item Generalized Anxiety Disorder questionnaire (GAD-7) is the screening tool most often described in clinical guidance for anxiety. It is used both to screen for anxiety disorders and to track their severity (guideline-anxiety-screening-and-first-line-care).\n\nScores on the GAD-7 are interpreted as follows:\n*   **5**: Mild anxiety\n*   **10**: Moderate anxiety\n*   **15**: Severe anxiety\n\nA score of 10 or greater is typically the threshold at which further assessment is recommended (guideline-anxiety-screening-and-first-line-care).\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
